23435	scriptorium	translation	And when they had begun (to recite) the Communion Service with great solemnity and reverence, behold, certain letters which had been sent by the hand of the captain of the lightly armed skirmishing troops, who was called Roumentros, who had been sent by the eparch of the frontier of \'Romania\', were delivered to the Emperor, and they contained the following message:
